ia (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":1},{"y":1853,"t":"loss","x":"1853: 60 Indian cells and 20 Thai cells drop out of the shape; no opened page.","cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":1},{"y":1853,"t":"loss","x":"1853: Cliopatria hands the Mosquito shore to its Mosquito Kingdom row (1853-1859).","cp":"mosquito-kingdom","cpn":"Mosquito Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":1},{"y":1853,"t":"gain","x":"1853: the New Zealand cells grow from 44 to 948.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":1},{"y":1856,"t":"gain","x":"1856: Cliopatria extends New South Wales and Victoria to their full colonial areas.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_colonies","c":1},{"y":1857,"t":"gain","x":"1857: Cliopatria extends South Australia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_colonies","c":1},{"y":1858,"t":"gain","x":"1858: the Colony of British Columbia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":1859,"t":"gain","x":"1859: Queensland is separated from New South Wales.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_colonies","c":3},{"y":1860,"t":"gain","x":"1860: China cedes Kowloon.","cp":"qing-dynasty","cpn":"Qing dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":1860,"t":"loss","x":"1860: the Bay Islands are surrendered to Honduras.","cp":"honduras","cpn":"Honduras","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":1861,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1861: the Mosquito Coast protectorate ends.","cp":"mosquito-kingdom","cpn":"Mosquito Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":186