lution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":1984,"t":"loss","x":"1984: Brunei is independent.","cp":"sultanate-of-brunei","cpn":"Sultanate of Brunei","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","c":3},{"y":1997,"t":"loss","x":"1 July 1997: Hong Kong is handed to China.","m":7,"cp":"people-s-republic-of-china","cpn":"People's Republic of China","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Empire","c":3},{"y":2001,"t":"dissolve","x":"End of 2001: the remaining dependent territories pass to the British Overseas Territories, founded in 2002.","cp":"british-overseas-territories","cpn":"British Overseas Territories","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Overseas_Territories","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"War of the Spanish Succession","from":1704,"to":1714,"outcome":"The Treaty of Utrecht (11 April 1713 with France; the Spanish treaties later in 1713) gave Britain Gibraltar and Menorca from Spain and Nova Scotia, Newfoundland claims, Rupert's Land claims and the French part of Saint Kitts from France.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Utrecht"},{"name":"Seven Years' War","from":1756,"to":1763,"outcome":"Treaty of Paris, signed 10 February 1763: France ceded Canada, Cape Breton, eastern Louisiana and several Windward islands; Spain ceded Florida; Britain restored Havana, Manila, Guadeloupe, Martinique and Saint Lucia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1763)"},{"name":"American Revolutionary War","from":1776,"to":1783,"outcome":"Treaty of Paris, signed 3 September 1783: Britain recognised the United States ('free, sovereign, and independent states') with the Great Lakes and Mississippi line; East and West Florida and Menorca went to Spain; Tobago and Senegal to France; Bahamas…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1783)"},{"name":"French Revolutionary Wars","from":1793,"to":1802,"outcome":"Treaty of Amiens, signed 25 March 1802: Britain returned the Cape Colony and most of Dutch Guiana and Menorca but kept Ceylon and Trinidad.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Amiens"},{"name":"Napoleonic Wars","from":1803,"to":1815,"outcome":"Britain took Mauritius (1810) and Java (1811); the Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 13 August 1814 returned the Dutch colonies except the Cape Colony, which was ceded, with trading rights in Demerara, Essequibo and Berbice; Java went back in 1816 (TE).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Dutch_Treaty_of_1814"},{"name":"First Opium War","from":1841,"to":1843,"outcome":"Britain seized Hong Kong Island (BE: 'the seizure by Britain of Hong Kong Island'); TE: occupied 1841, Crown colony 1843-1982.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire"},{"name":"Mesopotamian campaign","from":1914,"to":1918,"outcome":"British landings at Fao (6 November 1914) and Basra (22 November 1914), Kut lost 29 April 1916, Baghdad taken 11 March 1917, Mudros 30 October 1918, Mosul 14 November 1918; the campaign ended with a British mandate over Mesopotamia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamian_campaign"},{"name":"Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran","from":1941,"to":1942,"outcome":"Invasion 25 August 1941, ceasefire 29-30 August, Reza Shah's abdication 16 September, tripartite treaty 29 January 1942; the British held southern Iran (south of Hamadan and Qazvin) until the Allied withdrawal of March 1946.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Soviet_invasion_of_Iran"},{"name":"Pacific War","from":1942,"to":1945,"outcome":"Hong Kong, Malaya and the Straits Settlements were under Japanese occupation 1942-1945 and under British military administration 1945-1946 (TE).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire"}],"certainty":[{"from":1704,"to":1900,"level":"soft","note":"Colonial frontiers are approximate: a scatter of coastal settlements, plantation districts and trading posts, with the interior lines of North America, the Hudson Bay shore, Australia's interior and the Canadian north undrawn by treaty."},{"from":1901,"to":2001,"level":"sharp","note":"Dominion, colony and treaty-port borders are fixed by statute or treaty (Labrador by the 11 March 1927 decision, CAN)."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Empire","title":"British Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Utrecht","title":"Treaty of Utrecht"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1763)","title":"Treaty of Paris (1763)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1783)","title":"Treaty of Paris (1783)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Amiens","title":"Treaty of Amiens"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Dutch_Treaty_of_1814","title":"Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1814"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_Canada","title":"Territorial evolution of Canada"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_colonies","title":"Australian colonies"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Territorial_evolution_of_the_British_Empire","title":"Territorial evolution of the British Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamian_campaign","title":"Mesopotamian campaign"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Soviet_invasion_of_Iran","title":"Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aden_Protectorate","title":"Aden Protectorate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statute_of_Westminster_1931","title":"Statute of Westminster 1931"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglo-Iraqi_War","title":"Anglo-Iraqi War"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Iraq","title":"Kingdom of Iraq"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_of_Paris_(1783)","title":"Peace of Paris (1783)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Louis,_Senegal","title":"Saint-Louis, Senegal"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invasion_of_Martinique_(1809)","title":"Invasion of Martinique (1809)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invasion_of_